#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:4
msgid "XR on visionOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:6
msgid "To use the XR mode on visionOS, start by :ref:`setting up XR <doc_setting_up_xr>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:8
msgid "enable **XR shaders**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:9
msgid "add an :ref:`class_XROrigin3D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:10
msgid "add an :ref:`class_XRCamera3D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:12
msgid "You can initialize the visionOS XR interface similarly to any other :ref:`class_XRInterface`. In your viewport, enable ``use_xr``, enable ``use_hdr_2d``, and set ``vrs_mode`` to ``Viewport.VRS_XR``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:27
msgid "Hand and controller tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:29
msgid "You can enable hand and controller tracking in the project settings. visionOS will show a prompt asking for authorization when the game is launched. You can customize the prompt's message, in the export settings, to explain why your game needs hand or controller tracking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:34
msgid "The Godot nodes to use controller and hand tracking are the same as the other XRInterfaces: :ref:`class_XRController3D`, :ref:`class_XRHandTracker`, and :ref:`class_XRHandModifier3D`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:39
msgid "Transparent background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:41
msgid "When using **Mixed** immersion, the game is displayed as alpha-premultiplied on top of your physical surroundings. To get a fully transparent background, use a black background color with an alpha of 0. Any color other than black will render as additive on top of passthrough, even if alpha is 0."
msgstr ""

