#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:66
msgid "If you are using a colored background (either a flat color or a custom sky), make sure to :ref:`write to the depth buffer <doc_visionos_sky_depth_write>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:70
msgid "Mobile renderer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:72
msgid "The immersive mode on visionOS only supports the Mobile renderer. The game will fall back to the Mobile renderer, even if your project is configured to use Forward+."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:75
msgid "However, you might want to increase the :ref:`quality of shadows <doc_lights_and_shadows_shadow_filter_mode>` in the **Project Settings** since Godot's default quality for shadows is lower on mobile."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:79
msgid "Depth Re-projection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:81
msgid "visionOS uses the depth buffer of your rendered scene to re-project frames when the game doesn't render at the display's refresh rate. Be mindful of this when rendering transparent objects: write to the depth buffer for opaque parts that should be re-projected but do not write to the depth buffer for transparent or invisible objects that are less opaque than their background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:87
msgid "For transparent objects on top of the passthrough background (such as particles or :ref:`glow <doc_environment_and_post_processing_glow>`), make sure that at least one layer is writing depth, to avoid having :ref:`the content be discarded <doc_visionos_sky_depth_write>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:92
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:97
msgid "Block-shaped artifacts around edges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:101
msgid "If you see block-shaped artifacts around the edges, this is because Godot's sky shader does not write to depth and visionOS only displays content that has written depth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:104
msgid "Fix this by doing one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:106
msgid "Make the sky black if you want a transparent background."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:107
msgid "Add a full-screen quad that writes depth to the background, if you want to render a virtual sky (opaque or semi-transparent)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:110
msgid "To write depth to the sky, add a :ref:`class_MeshInstance3D` with the following shader:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:113
msgid "depth.gdshader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:134
msgid "And the following geometry:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:140
msgid "|depth_geometry|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:143
msgid "depth_geometry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:140
msgid "|depth_material|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:144
msgid "depth_material"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:146
msgid "This object does the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:148
msgid "renders in ``[-1.0; 1.0]`` in screen space."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:149
msgid "writes depth to ``0.00000001`` and alpha to ``1.0`` (or another alpha if you want semi-transparency)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:150
msgid "renders as the first transparent object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:151
msgid "never gets culled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:153
msgid "This is similar to doing :ref:`post-processing <doc_advanced_postprocessing>` in Godot, but is just writing depth and alpha."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:157
msgid "Camera near plane"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:159
msgid "visionOS (and more specifically `CompositorServices <https://developer.apple.com/documentation/compositorservices>`_) requires the near plane of the :ref:`class_XRCamera3D` to be at least 0.1 meters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:162
msgid "If you use a value below 0.1, the scene won't render. To solve this:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:164
msgid "increase the near value of you *XRCamera3D* to be ``0.1`` or greater."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:165
msgid "take into account the *world_scale* (including floating-point precision errors): ``znear = 0.1 * world_scale + margin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:166
msgid "make sure that the *XRCamera3D* is the current camera, because Godot derives the near/far planes from the camera on your viewport, which might not be the *XRCamera3D*. You can check the current camera with ``get_viewport().get_camera_3d()``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:171
msgid "Crash after freezing for 2 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:173
msgid "On visionOS, the OS kills CompositorServices apps if they hang for more than 2 seconds (except on the first frame)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:176
msgid "Godot does not currently support loading shaders in the background without freezing the render thread; you can fix this error by loading all your shaders upfront in the first scene of your Godot game."
msgstr ""

#: ../../docs/tutorials/xr/visionos_intro.rst:182
msgid "The 2 seconds timeout does not apply when the app is attached to Xcode. So make sure to test your game without launching from Xcode, before sharing it with more people, especially if it has long loading times."
msgstr ""
